> String.trim

    String.trim(text : String) : String

Without leading and trailing whitespace: the graphemes whose first code point is
White_Space, as `Char.isSpace` says. It is `trimStart` then `trimEnd`, a pair
the library keeps named (report Appendix E.0 rule 4).

Examples

    String.trim("  hi\n")
    // => "hi"

    String.trim("\u{a0}a\u{3000}")
    // => "a"
> no command :zz; :help lists them
> no command :help\tme; :help lists them
> :b is :bindings or :browse
> :f is :faults or :forget
> :type takes an expression
> no module Nope is in scope
> aaaa is not a module name: each segment of one is words beginning with a capital letter, as in Http.Parser or OrderedSet
> no module Nope under the source root or on the load path
> List is the standard library's, in scope from the start
> :reload takes no argument
> no documentation for Nope.nope
